<ArticleLayout title="Editorial policy" description="Our standards for independence, sourcing, authorship, updates, corrections, comparisons, and financial YMYL content." verifiedAt="2026-10-12" effective="Publication standards and correction log updated October 12, 2026">
  <h2>Independence</h2>
  <p>Child Savings Lab is an independent educational site. It is not part of the U.S. government, the Trump Accounts program, an investment adviser, a tax firm, or a law firm.</p>
  <h2>Evidence</h2>
  <p>Material federal-rule claims should link to primary government material. We label final guidance, form instructions, technical releases, and proposed regulations distinctly. Publication and verification dates are not interchangeable.</p>
  <h2>Authorship and review</h2>
  <p>Content is maintained by the independent publisher using the primary sources linked on each page. It has not been reviewed or signed off by a licensed attorney, CPA, CFP professional, or benefits specialist. We do not claim credentials or professional review that has not occurred.</p>
  <p>Research organization, drafting, software development, and testing use AI assistance. Automated output can be wrong; passing a test is not licensed-professional review or a guarantee of accuracy. “Published by Child Savings Lab” identifies this publication, not a named expert or a review team. The independent publisher is the editorial contact through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
  <h2>Comparisons and monetization</h2>
  <p>Purpose and user fit—not commission—determine comparison structure. If affiliate relationships are added later, they will be disclosed near relevant links and will not purchase rankings.</p>
  <h2 id="corrections">Corrections and updates</h2>
  <p>Substantive corrections should update the underlying rule, affected tools, tests, page copy, and verification date. Readers may report issues through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
  <h3>October 12, 2026</h3>
  <ul>
